            <fr:title text="What is elaboration?">What is elaboration?</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Elaboration is the process of producing <fr:link href="/000P/" title="Syntax" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/000P/" display-uri="000P" type="local">syntax</fr:link> from <fr:link href="/000Q/" title="Notation" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/000Q/" display-uri="000Q" type="local">notation</fr:link>, reporting <fr:link href="/000U/" title="Diagnostics" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/000U/" display-uri="000U" type="local">diagnostics</fr:link> to the user when the user’s intent as expressed through notation is not compatible with the rules of the type theory.</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
                <fr:uri>https://coln-project.github.io/000P/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>000P</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/000P/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Syntax">Syntax</fr:title>
                <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>Syntax is a data type in the Coln compiler, the elements of which are a compressed form for correct <fr:link href="/derivation/" title="Derivation" uri="https://coln-project.github.io/derivation/" display-uri="derivation" type="local">derivations</fr:link> in the Coln type theory.</html:p>
                <html:p>The process of elaboration ensures that any syntax produced does in fact refer uniquely to some derivation.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors />
